// =====================================================
// N8N WORKFLOW: PAPER MONITOR                                [P-13]
// A NEW, separate workflow (not part of the main signal workflow).
// A failure here never affects signals or Telegram, and vice versa.
//
// NOTE: these are N8N UI settings, not a Code node — except
//       "PAPER CANDLE NORMALIZER", whose code is in monitor/PAPER CANDLE NORMALIZER.
// Requires 003_engine.sql (Part 4 section) in Supabase.
// =====================================================

// ── 0. WORKFLOW SETTINGS ──────────────────────────────
//
// Name:             PAPER MONITOR
// Settings → Timezone:        Europe/Sofia
// Settings → Execution Order: v1 (recommended)
// Credential:  reuse "Supabase service_role (crypto)" (Custom Auth, see
//              row4/SUPABASE SIGNAL INSERT — N8N CONFIG, section 0).
// Base URL below: https://<PROJECT_REF>.supabase.co/rest/v1
//
// Canvas:
//
//   Schedule (HH:05)
//     → Get Targets            (HTTP POST rpc/paper_get_monitor_targets)
//     → Has Targets?           (IF count > 0)        false → end
//     → Split Out Targets      (Split Out: targets)
//     → Binance Klines 1h      (HTTP GET, per symbol)
//     → PAPER CANDLE NORMALIZER (Code, all items → 1 item)
//     → Ingest Candles         (HTTP POST rpc/paper_ingest_candles)
//     → Evaluate Positions     (HTTP POST rpc/paper_evaluate_positions)
//     → Notify?                (IF notify && events)  false → end
//     → Split Out Events → Telegram Exit Message

// ── 1. Schedule Trigger ───────────────────────────────
// Trigger Interval: Hours · Hours Between Triggers: 1 · Trigger at Minute: 5
// (~720 executions / month. If the N8N quota is too small, use every 2 hours:
//  the cursor catches up all missed candles, results are identical — spec 2.2.)

// ── 2. HTTP Request: "Get Targets" ────────────────────
// Method: POST
// URL:    {BASE}/rpc/paper_get_monitor_targets
// Authentication: Generic Credential Type → Custom Auth → Supabase service_role (crypto)
// Headers: Content-Type: application/json
// Body (JSON): {}
// Response: one item → { "count": 2, "targets": [ {"symbol":"BTCUSDT","start_time_ms":1763722800000}, ... ] }
// Settings → Retry On Fail: ON, Max Tries 3, Wait 2000 ms

// ── 3. IF: "Has Targets?" ─────────────────────────────
// Condition (Number): {{ $json.count }}  is greater than  0
// TRUE  → Split Out Targets
// FALSE → (unconnected) — execution ends, nothing to monitor

// ── 4. Split Out: "Split Out Targets" ─────────────────
// Field To Split Out: targets
// Include: No Other Fields
// Output: one item per symbol → { symbol, start_time_ms }
// The node NAME must be exactly "Split Out Targets" (the normalizer reads it).

// ── 5. HTTP Request: "Binance Klines 1h" ──────────────
// Method: GET
// URL:    https://api.binance.com/api/v3/klines
// Send Query Parameters (Using Fields Below):
//   symbol    = {{ $json.symbol }}
//   interval  = 1h
//   startTime = {{ $json.start_time_ms }}
//   limit     = 1000
// Authentication: None (public endpoint — same host as the main workflow)
// Options:
//   Batching:  Items per Batch 5 · Batch Interval 1000 ms   (5 requests / second)
//   Response → Include Response Headers and Status: ON     (REQUIRED by the normalizer)
//   Response → Response Format: JSON
//   Timeout: 15000 ms
// Settings:
//   Retry On Fail: ON · Max Tries 3 · Wait Between Tries 2000 ms
//   On Error: Continue   (one bad symbol must not stop the run;
//                         it is reported in failed_symbols → run status PARTIAL)

// ── 6. Code: "PAPER CANDLE NORMALIZER" ────────────────
// Mode: Run Once for All Items · Language: JavaScript
// Code: paste monitor/PAPER CANDLE NORMALIZER
// Output: ONE item { candles: [...], failed_symbols: [...], requested, candles_count, dropped_unclosed }

// ── 7. HTTP Request: "Ingest Candles" ─────────────────
// Method: POST
// URL:    {BASE}/rpc/paper_ingest_candles
// Authentication: Custom Auth → Supabase service_role (crypto)
// Headers: Content-Type: application/json
// Body Content Type: JSON · Specify Body: Using JSON
// JSON (expression):
//   {{ JSON.stringify({ p_candles: $json.candles }) }}
// Response: { "received": n, "valid": n, "inserted": n, "updated": n }
// Settings → Retry On Fail: ON, Max Tries 3, Wait 2000 ms
// (Safe to retry: upsert by symbol + open_time.)

// ── 8. HTTP Request: "Evaluate Positions" ─────────────
// Method: POST
// URL:    {BASE}/rpc/paper_evaluate_positions
// Authentication: Custom Auth → Supabase service_role (crypto)
// Headers: Content-Type: application/json
// JSON (expression):
//   {{ JSON.stringify({ p_failed_symbols: $('PAPER CANDLE NORMALIZER').first().json.failed_symbols }) }}
// Response: { status: OK|PARTIAL|ERROR|SKIPPED_LOCKED, run_id, evaluated, candles_used,
//             events_created, closed, events: [...], notify_telegram_on_exit, errors: [...] }
// Settings → Retry On Fail: OFF  (a second call while the first still runs would just
//            return SKIPPED_LOCKED; the next hourly run catches up anyway)
// The function never raises: problems come back as status PARTIAL / ERROR and are
// stored in paper_monitor_runs.

// ── 9. IF: "Notify?" (optional exit notifications) ────
// Condition (Boolean): {{ $json.notify_telegram_on_exit === true && $json.events.length > 0 }}  is true
// Controlled in Supabase:  update paper_config set notify_telegram_on_exit = true where id = 1;
// TRUE  → Split Out Events
// FALSE → (unconnected)

// ── 10. Split Out: "Split Out Events" → Telegram: "Telegram Exit Message" ──
// Split Out field: events
// Telegram node: same bot credential / chat as the main workflow
// Text (expression):
//   📄 PAPER {{ $json.symbol }} {{ $json.direction }} — {{ $json.event_type }}
//   @ {{ Number($json.fill_price) }} | net {{ Number($json.net_usd).toFixed(2) }} $
// Settings → On Error: Continue  (a Telegram failure must not mark the run failed)

// ── 11. FIRST RUN CHECK (U) ───────────────────────────
// With at least one OPEN paper position (after a real signal, or a test signal):
//   1. Execute the workflow manually.
//   2. Get Targets shows count ≥ 1; Binance returns 200; normalizer logs candles.
//   3. In Supabase:
//        select * from paper_monitor_runs order by id desc limit 3;        -- a new row, status OK
//        select symbol, count(*), max(open_time) from paper_candles group by 1;
//        select id, symbol, status, last_evaluated_open_time, tp_hits, remaining_pct
//          from paper_positions where status in ('OPEN','CLOSED') order by id desc limit 10;
//   4. Execute again immediately: no new events, candles_used = 0 (idempotent).
// Then activate the workflow (toggle "Active").
